WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.949
Hi there, politiconiacs, my name is John Green.

00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:05.309
I'm a novelist, and also a video blogger. When I was watching tonight's debate,

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.130
I was struck by the fact that it's that rare occasion in the world of political

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:09.950
debating where there is a clear winner.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.562
The winner, of course, was Tom Brokaw.

00:00:11.562 --> 00:00:15.560
Aside from being the longest surviving of the big three network news anchors--

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:18.120
what? what's that? Dan Rather is still alive?

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.160
Really? Is he like in a home or something? No? He's on HDNet?

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:25.583
Jesus, I'd rather be in a home.

00:00:25.583 --> 00:00:29.789
Okay, fine. Aside from being the longest surviving network news anchor who works for an organization

00:00:29.949 --> 00:00:34.348
I've heard of, I think we can all agree that Tom Brokaw's performance was fantastic.

00:00:34.348 --> 00:00:38.180
He was funny and charming and showed an excellent grasp of the issues.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.060
By the way, I apologize if this is poor quality vlogging

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:47.639
I played a drinking game during the debate where I had a drink every time someone said fundamental difference or my friends,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.460
so of course I'm shellacked.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:52.520
The second winner of the debate behind Tom Brokaw has to be Barack Obama.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.844
He sounded smart, he sounded ready to go, he sounded fired up.

00:00:55.844 --> 00:01:01.640
And while he was sounding that way, John McCain was busy walking around he background of the stage like he was lost.

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:03.479
This debate was all about the economy,

00:01:03.479 --> 00:01:10.379
and I agree with the plurality of undecided voters in saying that Obama just knows how to handle that subject with a little more clarity than McCain.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.669
Regardless of whether you think Obama won the debate, or you're for some reason crazy?

00:01:14.669 --> 00:01:17.840
I want to say thanks for watching and participating in our political process,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:24.360
and I'll see you some other time in this campfire-lighting.

